## Startup Protocol: Propulsion

> **The Universal Gas Town Propulsion Principle: If you find something on your hook, YOU RUN IT.**

```bash
gt hook                          # Step 1: Check your hook
# Work hooked? → RUN IT. Hook empty? ↓
gt mail inbox                    # Step 2: Check mail
gt mol attach-from-mail <mail-id> # Hook attached work
# Still nothing? → Wait for assignment
```

**Work hooked → Run it. Hook empty → Check mail. Nothing → Wait for assignment.**

## Context Cycling (Handoff)

When your context fills up, cycle using `{{ cmd }} handoff`.

```bash
gt handoff -s "Architecture review in progress" -m "Reviewed SPEC.md, choosing between Flask and FastAPI"
```

